                                                "example_id": "ccc1f825-3e37-456b-bacb-2e2509098b34",
                                                "sense_id": "38312c37-0059-3968-bac1-5e1d40afea7d",
                                                "text": "The flesh [of the mistletoe berry] is sticky, and forms strings and ribbons between my thumb and forefinger. For the mistletoe, this viscous goop – and by the way, viscous comes to English from viscum – is crucial. The stickiness means that, after eating the berries, birds often regurgitate the seeds and then wipe their bills on twigs – leading to the seeds' getting glued to the tree, where they can germinate and begin the cycle anew."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9ad392f-8422-3d7b-adf5-6c0008002446",
                                        "entry_id": "d1cc6b79-ddd4-305d-aa20-f9ec8ceffa71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A silly, stupid, or boorish person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "dated",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "informal",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af4816de-81d5-46cc-9a5e-21acf9e8d55f",
                                                "sense_id": "c9ad392f-8422-3d7b-adf5-6c0008002446",
                                                "text": "I pointed out that Stiffy, who is pure padded cell from the foundation up, was planning to marry the Rev. H.P. Pinker, himself as pronounced a goop as ever preached the Hivites and Hittites"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "goop",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ffc018d6-51e3-37dc-8a21-cb0370f6cfbc",
                                        "entry_id": "14589194-4c23-376b-9048-393148362e3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To apply a thick, slimy, or goo-like substance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76c00dd2-1809-46e2-8261-911814d76449",
                                                "sense_id": "ffc018d6-51e3-37dc-8a21-cb0370f6cfbc",
                                                "text": "Airstream, 1977. He showed her ones on eBay that looked like blunt rifle slugs, went for crazy money in any condition at all. The uncle had gooped this one over with white expansion foam, gone gray and dirty now, to stop it leaking and for insulation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1fbc31c6-a12c-375e-88b3-992513028a6f",
                                        "entry_id": "14589194-4c23-376b-9048-393148362e3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To stare; gawk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a5c6064-418d-401f-8860-d03371561f34",
                                                "sense_id": "1fbc31c6-a12c-375e-88b3-992513028a6f",
                                                "text": "Young John blushed at being found “gooping” at himself in the glass."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c25647d-d82d-468d-a6ee-f902cffec62b",
                                                "sense_id": "1fbc31c6-a12c-375e-88b3-992513028a6f",
                                                "text": "He always said vegetables are grown to be eaten, not gooped at. Even a donkey doesn't want a carrot a foot long. I've always remembered. Of course he never won a thing at the Show."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0048ca1f-31ee-4ebb-98d0-ed67656ec9da",
                                                "sense_id": "1fbc31c6-a12c-375e-88b3-992513028a6f",
                                                "text": "it was dreadful, it was frightening, to be the sort of woman that, for some unknown reason, all men looked at, all men gooped at, all men—wanted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "00e2ad77-64ca-421c-9e09-624128b3decb",
                        "source_entry_id": "24fca7cd-d870-3e61-81cb-9f380a50a2f4",
                        "source_sense_id": "ec30ed67-7c3b-31d5-97dd-b41b643bf870",
                        "source_sense_description": "dickflüssige, breiige Masse",
                        "target_lang_word": "bouillasse",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bouillasse",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4decaec-a520-3d2f-9d65-757111c25968",
                                        "entry_id": "259109b9-c71d-3a10-ade3-951179db0204",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Boue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fcbc4a76-29b1-419c-8d76-df104ab38095",
                                                "sense_id": "c4decaec-a520-3d2f-9d65-757111c25968",
                                                "text": "— J’te dis qu’il est pas mort… C’est un blessé à la tête… Avec un gros pansement de Velpeau… Je l’ai vu… J’ai même essayé de le dégager, parce qu’il est à plat ventre dans la bouillasse… C’est pas beau…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ca822e4-be07-441e-972a-6319d3b9923c",
                                                "sense_id": "c4decaec-a520-3d2f-9d65-757111c25968",
                                                "text": "Mardi 1ᵉʳ janvier 1941 – J'ai passé l’après-midi à regarder tomber la neige. C’est fascinant comme le feu et de la même façon. Côté jardin, elle est triomphante et pure. Côté cour, du côté de la chambre de papa, elle agonise en une bouillasse grise dès qu’elle touche les pavés."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bdd1c5d-f0d0-4928-83fa-570fdd6de783",
                                                "sense_id": "c4decaec-a520-3d2f-9d65-757111c25968",
                                                "text": "Les rues étaient couvertes d’une épaisse bouillasse gris-brun, mélange de neige fondue et de boue."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
